    <h1>People Sitting on the Streets of Ginza Spark Debate</h1>

    <h2>Visitors Need Places to Rest</h2>
    <p>Ginza is a popular shopping area in Tokyo. Recently, some visitors have been sitting on the ground because they cannot find a place to rest.</p>
    <p>Some tourists walk for a long time and become tired. Cafes and restaurants may be full, and there are not enough benches in the area.</p>

    <h2>A Visitor's Opinion</h2>
    <p>A visitor from Malaysia said that she had walked for about an hour after visiting Osaka. She explained: "I would be happy if there were more benches where I could take a break."</p>
    <p>Having more places to sit could make visiting Ginza more comfortable for tourists.</p>

    <h2>Why Are There So Few Benches?</h2>
    <p>According to the police, adding benches is not easy. Ginza cares about its city image and the appearance of its streets. There is also limited space.</p>
    <p>Sitting on the street is not automatically illegal. However, it may become a problem if people block pedestrians or interfere with store businesses. Everyone needs to use public spaces safely and considerately.</p>

